# Malaria Cell Classifier

A web app that classifies blood smear cell images as Parasitized or 
Uninfected using a CNN trained on the NIH malaria cell image dataset.

## How it works
- **Model**: Lightweight CNN (Conv2D → MaxPool ×3 → GlobalAveragePooling 
  → Dense) trained on ~27,000 labeled cell images from the NIH malaria 
  dataset. Achieves ~95% validation accuracy.
- **Backend**: FastAPI serves the model via a /predict endpoint.
- **Frontend**: Plain HTML/CSS/JS — drag-and-drop image upload, styled result card.

## Architecture
model/ → training + inference logic
backend/ → FastAPI server
frontend/ → static UI

